### Attendance Intelligence API examples (VS Code "REST Client" / JetBrains HTTP client)
# Full spec: docs/openapi.json, Swagger UI at http://localhost:8000/docs
# Dev tokens exist only when APP_ENV is dev or test.

@base = http://localhost:8000

### Personas (dev/test only)
GET {{base}}/v1/auth/personas

### Token for a persona -> copy access_token into @token
# a_hr_admin, a_eng_manager, a_hr_manager, a_employee_e001, a_reviewer, a_auditor,
# b_manager, b_reviewer, x_other_product
# @name login
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/dev-token
Content-Type: application/json

{"persona": "a_eng_manager"}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### Who am I (what the gateway will enforce)
GET {{base}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Health (deep: database, vector, embeddings, cache, queue, OCR, providers + breakers)
GET {{base}}/v1/health/deep

### Upload a file (async; poll the job). Manager/HR admin only.
POST {{base}}/v1/ingest
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=b

--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="logical_name"

tenant_a_sep
--b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="tenant_a_sep_v2.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

< ../data/generated/tenant_a_sep_v2.csv
--b--

### Job status (replace the id)
GET {{base}}/v1/jobs/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Failed-file queue
GET {{base}}/v1/jobs?status=failed
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Structured question (answer + citations + confidence)
# @name q1
POST {{base}}/v1/query
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "Who was present on 1 September 2026?"}

### Aggregate
POST {{base}}/v1/query
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "What was Engineering's average attendance % in September?", "include_debug": true}

### Hybrid evidence question
POST {{base}}/v1/query
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "Show evidence that Alice was present on 3 Sep"}

### Unavailable (no data in scope)
POST {{base}}/v1/query
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "What was Alice's attendance in December 2027?"}

### Another tenant's employee: identical to an unknown name
POST {{base}}/v1/query
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "What was John Carter's attendance?"}

### Entity outside the token -> 403 CONTEXT_MISMATCH
POST {{base}}/v1/query
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "HR attendance in September?", "filters": {"entity_id": "hr"}}

### Stored answer by request id (404 outside your scope)
GET {{base}}/v1/query/{{q1.response.body.request_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Export the answer's evidence (json | xlsx | pdf); header X-Export-Checksum
POST {{base}}/v1/export
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"source": "query", "request_id": "{{q1.response.body.request_id}}", "format": "json"}

### Export records with filters
POST {{base}}/v1/export
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"source": "records", "format": "xlsx", "filters": {"date_from": "2026-09-14", "date_to": "2026-09-18", "status": "absent"}}

### Feedback (reviewer or hr_admin token): correction + ideal output for a previous answer
POST {{base}}/v1/feedback
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "original_request_id": "req_...",
  "feedback": "State the date range and how the percentage was calculated.",
  "ideal_final_output": "Engineering attendance from 01/09/2026 to 30/09/2026 was 91.83%, calculated from 95.5 present employee-days out of 104 scheduled employee-days.",
  "approve": true
}

### Feedback examples and versions in scope
GET {{base}}/v1/feedback
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deactivate / roll back an example
POST {{base}}/v1/feedback/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/rollback
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Audit trail for one request (auditor or hr_admin token)
GET {{base}}/v1/audit?request_id={{q1.response.body.request_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
